title: The Rote Fahne's Line
subtitle: The party paper's front page tells the members what the party thinks.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: rf_party
view-if: rf_editorial_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; rf_editorial_timer = 3

= The Rote Fahne's Line

The editors want a clear line for the coming weeks. Every faction will read the paper looking for itself.

- @front
- @fire
- @theory

@front
title: An open hand to <span class="p-spd">SPD</span> workers.
subtitle: Better relations with the SPD; pleases the <span class="f-right">Right</span>, angers the <span class="f-left">Left</span>.
on-arrival: {!
window.RF.lean(Q, {right: 3, left: -3});
Q.spd_relation += 4;
window.RF.normalize(Q);
!}

The paper calls on Social Democratic workers to join Communists in the factory councils and the price committees.

@fire
title: Fire at the Republic and its defenders.
subtitle: Raises the revolutionary mood; pleases the <span class="f-left">Left</span>, angers the <span class="f-right">Right</span>.
on-arrival: {!
window.RF.lean(Q, {left: 3, right: -3});
Q.rev_situation += 2;
Q.spd_relation -= 3;
window.RF.normalize(Q);
!}

The paper says the Republic is finished and asks who will inherit it.

@theory
title: Theory and education.
subtitle: Calms the factions a little.
on-arrival: {!
for (var f of window.RF.factions) { Q[f + '_dissent'] -= 2; }
window.RF.normalize(Q);
!}

Long articles on Marx and Lenin fill the inside pages. Nobody is offended; few are excited.
